	abstract = {Traceability information is essential for effective software maintenance and operation. In this study, we propose a traceability link recovery approach that leverages the capabilities of LLMs for linking requirements and source code. While LLMs demonstrate powerful language comprehension, they still have limitations in capturing domain-specific terminology. To overcome this limitation, we combine the semantic similarity extracted by LLMs with the textual similarity computed by an information retrieval (IR)-based method. Experimental results demonstrate that our proposed method improves the F1-score by up to 10.7 percentage points and MAP by up to 9.1 percentage points compared to state-of-the-art methods.  © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).},
