	abstract = {As systems engineering (SE) evolves, adaptability in managing requirements debt (RQ Debt) is crucial to reducing long-term project risk. This study explores the use of Intelligent Document Processing (IDP) and Large Language Models (LLMs) to detect RQ Debt in Systems Engineering Management Plans (SEMPs). Through ongoing interviews with SE professionals, we are developing an iterative RQ Debt Detection Guide while testing Chain-of-Thought (CoT) and In-Context Learning (ICL) for automated RQ Debt evaluation. Early results suggest CoT improves traceability, while ICL enhances contextual accuracy, though human validation is still needed. The next phase will incorporate expert feedback to refine the guide and establish a validation matrix, forming the foundation for future ML applications. © 2025 The Authors.},
