	abstract = {Traditional methods of analysing Software Requirements Specification (SRS) document analysis rely on manual processes, leading to challenges such as ambiguity, inconsistency, and incomplete specifications. In the rapidly evolving field of software engineering, the effective analysis of Software Requirements Specifications (SRS) is crucial for ensuring successful project outcomes. Our research introduces a tool that utilizes LangChain and GPT-4 to enhance the analysis of SRS documents. This advanced tool integrates state-of-the-art natural language processing techniques to automate the extraction, classification, and evaluation of requirements from complex SRS documents, leading to the implementation of CMMI levels 3 and 4 in an organization. By leveraging GPT-4’s contextual understanding and LangChain’s modular framework, our tool enhances the accuracy and efficiency of requirements analysis while strengthening knowledge and portfolio management practices. The overarching goal is to integrate AI-based tools from the early stages of a project, systematically improving processes in a quantifiable and traceable manner, thereby enabling software organizations to progress toward Capability Maturity Model Integration (CMMI) Levels 3 and 4. © 2025 IEEE.},
